Here is the PlantUML class diagram:
@startuml
class Theater {
  - location: String
}

class Play {
  - name: String
  - type: String (musical or opera)
  - authors: Author[]
  - participants: Participant[]
  - sessions: Session[]
}

class Author {
  - name: String
  - plays: Play[]
}

class Participant {
  - name: String
  - plays: Play[]
  - sessions: Session[]
}

class Person {
  +name: String
}

class Session {
  - beginTime: Date
  - endTime: Date
  - play: Play
  - participant: Participant
}

Theater o--* Play : can_play
Play ..> Author : written_by
Author o--* Play : has_written
Play o--* Participant : has_participant
Participant o--* Session : acts_in
Session ..> Play : part_of
Person <|-- Author
Person <|-- Participant

@enduml
Note: The `o--` and `..>` symbols are used to represent relationships between classes. The `+` symbol is used to indicate that a class has an attribute, while the `-` symbol indicates that it's a field (i.e., not a method).